<article class="env-lemma" id="0FB7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FB7">Lemma <span data-tag="0FB7">42.50.8</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0GUJ" data-tag="0GUJ">42.50.1</a> assume $Z \subset Z' \subset X$ where $Z'$ is a closed subscheme of $X$. Then $P_ p(Z' \to X, E) = (Z \to Z')_* \circ P_ p(Z \to X, E)$, resp. $c_ p(Z' \to X, E) = (Z \to Z')_* \circ c_ p(Z \to X, E)$ (with $\circ $ as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0EPK" data-tag="0EPK">42.33.4</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The construction of $P_ p(Z' \to X, E)$, resp. $c_ p(Z' \to X, E)$ in Lemma <a href="/tag/0FB2" data-tag="0FB2">42.50.2</a> uses the exact same morphism $b : W \to \mathbf{P}^1_ X$ and perfect object $Q$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ W)$. Then we can use Lemma <a href="/tag/0FAI" data-tag="0FAI">42.47.5</a> to conclude. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>